      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1141739
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-25T15:45:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "just realized that we might want to build multiple keyboard ECs with touchpad firmwares in parallel, putting these in zmake command line is not a good choice, it\u0027s hard to pair the board name and fw path. I\u0027m planning to move this to kconfig, what do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "63449ca3_9c5fd386",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "90cd159a3da3bb5b0bd937c3af91e4c4207f5f35",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce9dffab_6c00f5ad",
        "filename": "zephyr/Kconfig.usb_update",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T02:50:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "kconfig sounds fine, but I think a new flashmap region for the hash is even better. it would allow setting the hash outside the build",
      "parentUuid": "82c4f83e_d59b4ca2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "90cd159a3da3bb5b0bd937c3af91e4c4207f5f35",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
